1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,490
Would you survive a zombie apocalypse? Be
honest.

2
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:08,259
You've played every zombie game ever made.
You're basically a soldier.

3
00:00:08,579 --> 00:00:13,342
Headshots? Easy. Infinite ammo? Easy.
Respawn? Always.

4
00:00:13,662 --> 00:00:17,200
But real life gives you one life, and no
save button.

5
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:21,767
I'm Coach Dex, and I have survived
fourteen zombie apocalypses.

6
00:00:22,087 --> 00:00:25,333
Okay, none. But I own a very loud whistle.

7
00:00:25,653 --> 00:00:28,637
[Maya, on the radio] Dad. You tripped over
a sofa yesterday.

8
00:00:28,957 --> 00:00:30,629
That was a very aggressive sofa.

9
00:00:30,949 --> 00:00:34,693
This video is sponsored by Not Dying. Now
with fewer bites.

10
00:00:35,013 --> 00:00:37,842
Not Dying is not a real product. Please
don't ask.

11
00:00:38,162 --> 00:00:41,026
Before we start, hit the like button. I
will wait.

12
00:00:41,346 --> 00:00:43,315
Oh. Hi, Steve.

13
00:00:43,435 --> 00:00:44,125
[Steve] Uhhhhh.

14
00:00:44,445 --> 00:00:48,375
Steve is a zombie. He has no plan. Today,
you will.

15
00:00:48,695 --> 00:00:52,575
Eight zombie situations. Two choices in
each one.

16
00:00:52,895 --> 00:00:56,627
Choice A is the video game way. Choice B
is what actually works.

17
00:00:56,947 --> 00:01:00,906
I died eight times making this video. Real
me is fine.

18
00:01:01,226 --> 00:01:01,926
Let's begin.

19
00:01:03,626 --> 00:01:05,723
[Game] Level one. The building.

20
00:01:06,043 --> 00:01:10,319
Day one. You're on the ninth floor, and
the lobby is full of zombies.

21
00:01:10,639 --> 00:01:14,001
Two ways down: an elevator, or a boring
old staircase.

22
00:01:14,321 --> 00:01:18,914
A, elevator. B, stairs. Pick one.

23
00:01:19,234 --> 00:01:24,653
Game brain says elevator. It is fast, it
is shiny, it has music.

24
00:01:24,973 --> 00:01:28,151
Ding! Floor three. The doors open...

25
00:01:28,471 --> 00:01:29,520
[Game] You died.

26
00:01:31,671 --> 00:01:33,823
In a game, that is a loading screen.

27
00:01:34,143 --> 00:01:36,984
In real life, the power dies between
floors.

28
00:01:37,304 --> 00:01:39,946
Now you are stuck in a metal box with one
door.

29
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:42,595
And every zombie knows exactly where it
opens.

30
00:01:42,915 --> 00:01:47,605
Choice B: the stairs. Boring, slow, and
full of doors.

31
00:01:47,925 --> 00:01:52,103
Close every door behind you. Each one
costs them time.

32
00:01:52,423 --> 00:01:56,482
And stairs let you stop, turn around, or
change your mind.

33
00:01:56,802 --> 00:02:01,166
An elevator has one exit. A staircase has
a door on every floor.

34
00:02:01,486 --> 00:02:05,087
Rule one: never enter a box with only one
door.

35
00:02:05,407 --> 00:02:08,424
Steve took the elevator. We do not talk
about Steve.

36
00:02:08,744 --> 00:02:10,820
[Game] Level two. The street.

37
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:14,903
Day two. A hundred zombies on the road,
and your car is dead.

38
00:02:15,223 --> 00:02:19,235
They are slow, but they are everywhere.
Run, or walk?

39
00:02:19,555 --> 00:02:23,735
A, sprint like a hero. B, walk like a
boring person.

40
00:02:24,055 --> 00:02:28,044
Game brain sprints. Stamina bar? Infinite.

41
00:02:28,364 --> 00:02:30,562
Legs? Also infinite.

42
00:02:30,882 --> 00:02:35,223
Sprinting means shouting. Every zombie in
town just heard you.

43
00:02:35,543 --> 00:02:37,281
[Game] You died. Again.

44
00:02:38,543 --> 00:02:40,927
In real life, there is no stamina bar.

45
00:02:41,247 --> 00:02:43,302
After four hundred meters, you're done.

46
00:02:43,622 --> 00:02:47,846
And wheezing like a broken vacuum cleaner
is not exactly stealth.

47
00:02:48,166 --> 00:02:51,471
Choice B: walk. Steady, quiet, along the
wall.

48
00:02:51,791 --> 00:02:56,201
Zombies hunt noise and motion. Be the most
boring thing on the street.

49
00:02:56,521 --> 00:03:00,737
Walking, you can go for hours. Sprinting?
About two minutes.

50
00:03:01,057 --> 00:03:03,754
Sprint: two minutes. Walk: all night.

51
00:03:04,074 --> 00:03:05,610
Rule two: be boring.

52
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:09,342
Steve sprinted. Steve fell over. Steve is
fine.

53
00:03:09,662 --> 00:03:11,948
[Game] Level three. The hideout.

54
00:03:12,268 --> 00:03:16,403
Day three. An empty apartment. Time to
hide.

55
00:03:16,723 --> 00:03:20,719
There is a closet right there. And a room
with two exits.

56
00:03:21,039 --> 00:03:23,494
Closet, or the room with two exits?

57
00:03:23,814 --> 00:03:27,809
Game brain loves closets. In games,
enemies never open them.

58
00:03:28,129 --> 00:03:31,430
So you hide. And the zombie opens the
door.

59
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:35,732
[Game] You died. Continue? Nine. Eight.
Seven.

60
00:03:36,350 --> 00:03:40,269
Real zombies don't read the rules. If they
hear you, they check everywhere.

61
00:03:40,589 --> 00:03:45,865
A closet is a coffin with a door. One way
in, one way out, and they are standing in it.

62
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:50,461
Choice B: two exits. Zombie comes in one
door, you go out the other.

63
00:03:50,781 --> 00:03:55,437
Stay quiet, stay near the exits, and
listen. Sound is your radar.

64
00:03:55,757 --> 00:03:56,873
Hide where you can leave.

65
00:03:57,357 --> 00:04:01,078
If you cannot leave, you are not hiding.
You are waiting.

66
00:04:01,398 --> 00:04:04,710
Closet: trapped. Two exits: alive.

67
00:04:05,030 --> 00:04:07,532
Rule three: never hide where you cannot
leave.

68
00:04:07,852 --> 00:04:11,729
Steve is also hiding. Behind a plant. It
is not working.

69
00:04:12,049 --> 00:04:14,303
[Game] Level four. The fight.

70
00:04:14,623 --> 00:04:19,457
Day four. Six zombies, one doorway, and
one baseball bat.

71
00:04:19,777 --> 00:04:23,972
Every game says: fight them. Swing the
bat. Be the hero.

72
00:04:24,292 --> 00:04:27,950
A, swing the bat. B, close the door.

73
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:32,318
Game brain swings. Combo times five.

74
00:04:32,638 --> 00:04:35,126
Health regenerates. You are a legend.

75
00:04:35,446 --> 00:04:38,084
Then the bat breaks, and nobody hands you
a new one.

76
00:04:38,404 --> 00:04:39,454
[Game] You died.

77
00:04:41,404 --> 00:04:46,092
Real fights have no health bar, no combo
meter, and a bat is just a stick.

78
00:04:46,412 --> 00:04:50,766
Six against one is not a fight. It is a
math problem, and you lose.

79
00:04:51,086 --> 00:04:55,967
Choice B: close the door. Lock it, wedge
it, put a chair under the handle.

80
00:04:56,287 --> 00:05:00,508
If one gets close, use something long: a
pole, a broom, a mop.

81
00:05:00,828 --> 00:05:01,944
Distance is armor.

82
00:05:02,428 --> 00:05:06,292
At a doorway, they come one at a time. But
walking away is better.

83
00:05:06,612 --> 00:05:10,074
Rule four: the best fight is the door you
close.

84
00:05:10,394 --> 00:05:13,401
Steve does not fight. Steve knocks.
Politely.

85
00:05:13,721 --> 00:05:15,819
[Game] Level five. The loot.

86
00:05:16,139 --> 00:05:21,509
Day five. A supermarket. Untouched. Every
shelf is full.

87
00:05:21,829 --> 00:05:26,269
Games say: take everything. Your bag has
ninety-nine slots.

88
00:05:26,589 --> 00:05:30,477
A, grab everything. B, carry ten kilos.

89
00:05:30,797 --> 00:05:35,205
Game brain fills every slot. Weight?
Infinite. Backpack? Magic.

90
00:05:35,525 --> 00:05:39,735
Congratulations, you are carrying a whole
supermarket. And you are slower than Steve.

91
00:05:40,055 --> 00:05:42,470
[Game] You were overencumbered. You died.

92
00:05:43,455 --> 00:05:48,406
In real life, a liter of water weighs
a kilo. At twenty-four kilos, you cannot run.

93
00:05:48,726 --> 00:05:53,798
Cans clank. Bags tear. Every step is loud.

94
00:05:54,118 --> 00:05:59,083
Choice B: ten kilos. Water, food, light,
first aid, charger.

95
00:05:59,403 --> 00:06:02,960
Pick light things that keep you alive.
Leave the television.

96
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:07,336
Ten kilos. You can walk all day, and you
can still run when you must.

97
00:06:07,656 --> 00:06:10,116
Rule five: weight is a zombie too.

98
00:06:10,436 --> 00:06:13,737
Steve took the television. Steve does not
have electricity.

99
00:06:14,057 --> 00:06:16,620
[Game] Level six. The night.

100
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:21,109
Day six. Night falls, and I have not slept
in two days.

101
00:06:21,429 --> 00:06:25,793
Games have save points. Lie down, press a
button, and everything is safe.

102
00:06:26,113 --> 00:06:30,194
A, sleep anywhere. B, sleep smart.

103
00:06:30,514 --> 00:06:35,083
Game brain sleeps on the street. Health
refills by morning. Probably.

104
00:06:35,403 --> 00:06:37,191
[Game] You died in your sleep.

105
00:06:38,603 --> 00:06:43,764
Real sleep is not a save point. It is the
most dangerous eight hours of your life.

106
00:06:44,084 --> 00:06:46,161
[Maya, on the radio] Dad? Did you sleep
yet?

107
00:06:46,281 --> 00:06:47,420
Working on it, kiddo.

108
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:51,841
Choice B: sleep smart. Two exits, so you
can always leave.

109
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:54,462
A string of tin cans across the door.

110
00:06:54,782 --> 00:06:57,290
Cheap, loud, and it never falls asleep.

111
00:06:57,610 --> 00:07:02,199
And a dog on watch. Respawn is on duty,
and he works for snacks.

112
00:07:02,519 --> 00:07:07,163
Cans rattle. Dog barks. You are awake, and
already leaving.

113
00:07:07,483 --> 00:07:12,157
Short naps, two exits, one alarm. Sleep in
pieces.

114
00:07:12,477 --> 00:07:16,192
Rule six: sleep with an alarm and an exit.

115
00:07:16,512 --> 00:07:18,715
We tested the alarm on Steve. It works.

116
00:07:19,035 --> 00:07:21,370
[Game] Level seven. The road.

117
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:26,552
Day seven. The highway runs straight to
the harbor. It is also a parking lot.

118
00:07:26,872 --> 00:07:30,000
A, the highway. B, the railway.

119
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:35,379
Game brain follows the glowing line on the
minimap. Straight down the highway. Easy.

120
00:07:35,699 --> 00:07:38,719
A thousand cars. A thousand hiding places.

121
00:07:39,039 --> 00:07:40,465
And every alarm goes off.

122
00:07:40,785 --> 00:07:42,523
[Game] You died. Again.

123
00:07:43,785 --> 00:07:49,305
Real highways are traffic jams with teeth.
Zombies hide behind every bumper.

124
00:07:49,625 --> 00:07:51,280
Choice B: the railway.

125
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:55,968
Open ground. Long sight lines. Nothing to
hide behind.

126
00:07:56,288 --> 00:08:01,158
At night: no flashlight. Light is a
loudspeaker. Let your eyes adjust.

127
00:08:01,478 --> 00:08:05,928
Follow the rails. They go where you are
going, and nobody parks on them.

128
00:08:06,248 --> 00:08:11,258
The railway is longer. But longer and
alive beats shorter and bitten.

129
00:08:11,578 --> 00:08:14,278
Rule seven: light is a loudspeaker.

130
00:08:14,598 --> 00:08:19,656
Steve found a flashlight. Steve turned it
on. Steve was very visible.

131
00:08:19,976 --> 00:08:22,076
[Game] Level eight. The rescue.

132
00:08:22,396 --> 00:08:26,638
Day eight. A helicopter! It is circling
the city, and it can see me.

133
00:08:26,958 --> 00:08:30,391
A, wait on the roof. B, run to the dock.

134
00:08:30,711 --> 00:08:32,472
Game brain waits on the roof.

135
00:08:32,792 --> 00:08:36,302
In games, the helicopter always lands at
the last second.

136
00:08:36,622 --> 00:08:40,023
The helicopter flies away. The zombies
arrive instead.

137
00:08:40,343 --> 00:08:42,577
[Game] You died. Final death.

138
00:08:43,743 --> 00:08:48,137
In real life, helicopters are rare, and
they do not land in a zombie city.

139
00:08:48,457 --> 00:08:51,552
It flies away. Nobody sees a waving man in
the dark.

140
00:08:51,872 --> 00:08:53,885
And the stairs behind you? Full.

141
00:08:54,205 --> 00:08:58,951
Choice B: go where the boats are. Water is
a wall zombies cannot cross.

142
00:08:59,271 --> 00:09:03,539
And use a signal mirror. A flash of
sunlight can be seen for miles.

143
00:09:03,859 --> 00:09:07,309
Zombies cannot swim. Steve checked.

144
00:09:07,629 --> 00:09:12,534
A boat. A real one. With someone on the
deck, waving.

145
00:09:12,854 --> 00:09:14,834
Rule eight: water is the wall.

146
00:09:15,154 --> 00:09:17,103
[Maya, on the radio] Dad! You are late!

147
00:09:17,423 --> 00:09:19,105
Sorry, sweetheart! Traffic!

148
00:09:19,425 --> 00:09:20,905
[Maya, on the radio] Did you take the
stairs?

149
00:09:21,025 --> 00:09:21,988
I took the stairs.

150
00:09:22,308 --> 00:09:25,694
Respawn! You made it too. Who is a good
boy?

151
00:09:26,014 --> 00:09:29,316
Oh, and Steve walked off the pier. He
cannot swim.

152
00:09:29,636 --> 00:09:34,496
Final score. Game: eight deaths. Real
life: zero.

153
00:09:34,816 --> 00:09:38,645
Because in a game, you respawn. In real
life, you prepare.

154
00:09:38,965 --> 00:09:41,977
Eight rules. Eight ways to stay alive.

155
00:09:44,165 --> 00:09:49,065
If you liked this, subscribe. If not,
Steve says hello.

156
00:09:49,385 --> 00:09:53,972
Next time: how to survive a robot
uprising. Game versus real life.

